{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"76fe9cdeeb689ff25fe8c473accc61acebeed146f931726d6be9cd7632606094","slug":"api.records","location":"/api/records.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Tax-Calculator Records","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Policy Simulation Library","given":"Policy Simulation","family":"Library"},"name":"Policy Simulation Library","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/main/docs/api/records.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/edit/main/docs/api/records.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"records.md","url":"/build/records-142ad2ebf244c67bb3dac2b68addad4c.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Documentation of the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"yBZaQZVMFA"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taxcalc.records","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"HEelqRkpFC"},{"type":"text","value":" module.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"azXVLZ7EIC"}],"key":"fmuzmJ1egP"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Records","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"tkPzTtXThL"}],"identifier":"records","label":"Records","html_id":"records","implicit":true,"key":"Gd0C5KesDV"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"class Records(data=None, start_year=None, gfactors=None, weights=None, adjust_ratios=None, exact_calculations=False, weights_scale=0.01)","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"F0YPRPuPfQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/records.py#L17","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"source","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"FhUGKXA4Xu"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/records.py#L17","data":{"kind":"file","org":"PSLmodels","repo":"Tax-Calculator","reference":"master","file":"taxcalc/records.py","from":17,"raw":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/master/taxcalc/records.py"},"internal":false,"protocol":"github","key":"jL08Wt2geL"}],"key":"jb7TkIpw5O"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"Records is a subclass of the abstract Data class, and therefore,\ninherits its methods (none of which are shown here).\n\nConstructor for the tax-filing-unit Records class.\n\nParameters\n----------\ndata: string or Pandas DataFrame or None\n    string describes CSV file in which records data reside;\n    DataFrame already contains records data;\n    default value is None.\n    NOTE: when using custom data, set this argument to a DataFrame.\n    NOTE: to use your own data for a specific year with Tax-Calculator,\n    be sure to read the documentation on creating your own data file and\n    then construct a Records object like this::\n\n        mydata = pd.read_csv(<mydata.csv>)\n        myrec = Records(data=mydata, start_year=<mydata_year>,\n                        gfactors=None, weights=None)\n\n    NOTE: data=None is allowed but the returned instance contains only\n    the data variable information in the specified VARINFO file.\n\nstart_year: integer or None\n    specifies calendar year of the input data;\n    default value is None.\n    Note that if specifying your own data (see above NOTE) as being\n    a custom data set, be sure to explicitly set start_year to the\n    custom data's calendar year.\n\ngfactors: GrowFactors class instance or None\n    containing record data growth (or extrapolation) factors.\n    default value is None.\n\nweights: Pandas DataFrame or None\n    DataFrame contains data weights;\n    None creates empty weights DataFrame;\n    default value is None\n    NOTE: when using custom weights, set this argument to a DataFrame.\n    NOTE: see weights_scale documentation below.\n\nadjust_ratios: Pandas DataFrame or None\n    DataFrame contains transposed/no-index adjustment ratios;\n    None creates empty adjustment-ratios DataFrame;\n    default value is None.\n    NOTE: when using custom ratios, set this argument to a DataFrame.\n    NOTE: if specifying a DataFrame, set adjust_ratios to my_df\n    defined as::\n\n        my_df = pd.read_csv('<my_ratios.csv>', index_col=0).transpose()\n\nexact_calculations: boolean\n    specifies whether or not exact tax calculations are done without\n    any smoothing of stair-step provisions in income tax law;\n    default value is false.\n\nweights_scale: float\n    specifies the weights scaling factor used to convert contents\n    of weights file into the s006 variable.  PUF and CPS input data\n    generated in the taxdata repository use a weights_scale of 0.01,\n    while TMD input data generated in the tax-microdata repository\n    use a 1.0 weights_scale value.\n    default value is 0.01.\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError:\n    if data is not the appropriate type.\n    if taxpayer and spouse variables do not add up to filing-unit total.\n    if dividends is less than qualified dividends.\n    if gfactors is not None or a GrowFactors class instance.\n    if start_year is not an integer.\n    if files cannot be found.\n\nReturns\n-------\nclass instance: Records\n\nNotes\n-----\nUse Records.cps_constructor() to get a Records object instantiated\nwith CPS input data developed in the taxdata repository.\n\nUse Records.puf_constructor() to get a Records object instantiated\nwith PUF input data developed in the taxdata repository.\n\nUse Records.tmd_constructor() to get a Records object instantiated\nwith TMD input data developed in the tax-microdata repository.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"nE1WthzpI1"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Records.cps_constructor","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"hDsL7HZ0Rw"}],"identifier":"records-cps-constructor","label":"Records.cps_constructor","html_id":"records-cps-constructor","implicit":true,"key":"d1uw1dEk58"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"def cps_constructor(data=None, gfactors=GrowFactors(), exact_calculations=False)","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"key":"aK8GPwYXxO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/records.py#L202","position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"source","position":{"start":{"line":110,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"key":"WyLOjCmS7r"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/blob/master/taxcalc/records.py#L202","data":{"kind":"file","org":"PSLmodels","repo":"Tax-Calculator","reference":"master","file":"taxcalc/records.py","from":202,"raw":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PSLmodels/Tax-Calculator/master/taxcalc/records.py"},"internal":false,"protocol":"github","key":"QvMNpe61ey"}],"key":"Ymv8Edfd0g"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"Static method returns a Records object instantiated with CPS\ninput data.  This is a convenience method that eliminates the\nneed to specify all the details of the CPS input data.","position":{"st